  {
    "index": 3,
    "hash": "jc0fFnN/uIFSMkTvcE3/yHmt1bg=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-19T11:30:47.019Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "BJSS was the UK's largest independent engineering consultancy and has been acquired; its stack is now CGI's. The record keeps it as a warning rather than as a target, because the independence that qualified it is gone and the technology direction is now set by the acquirer.\n\nThe detail that makes it a warning rather than simply a deletion is that it won a GBP 27.8m NHS Education for Scotland contract after the deal. Acquisition did not cost it the public-sector business; it cost this lead set an independent supplier. The pattern that follows is commercially relevant: the largest independent firms in these markets are the ones being bought, so a lead qualified on independence has a shelf life, and the independence field needs a date attached to it.\n\nIt sits at priority 9, do not pitch.\n\n---\n\n## Leads sharing this finding (1)\n\n**9 \u00b7 do not pitch**\n- BJSS (UK)\n\nVerbatim research text this claim was extracted from:\n\n> ACQUIRED. Was the UK's largest independent engineering consultancy. Won GBP 27.8m NHS Education for Scotland post-deal. Kept as a warning, not a target.",
        "updatedAt": "2026-08-19T11:30:47.019609Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-19T11:30:47.019613Z"
    }
  },
